No, a 1D array cannot be sliced like a[:,1] because a[:,1] is used for 2D arrays ,where : represents all rows and 1 represents
the second column. A 1D array has only one dimension and does not contain rows and columns,so using two indices causes an 
IndexError. For a 1D array, slicing can be done but by using a single index such as a[1] or a[1:3].
